                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d8415324-71df-3bac-8475-3cd41fe45e52",
                        "entry_id": "ba49c5d1-e9fd-334f-a181-1ff4de32e169",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. применявшееся в Древней Руси и многих странах Востока холодное оружие в виде короткой палки, на одном конце которой с помошью цепи или ремня прикреплён металлический шар, обычно с шипами, а на другом — петля, надевавшаяся на руку"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7db50b0e-6831-4307-bf84-b87b1e2c43ea",
                                "sense_id": "d8415324-71df-3bac-8475-3cd41fe45e52",
                                "text": "У иных молодцов были привешены к бедрам сабли, другие мотали в руках кистени или опирались на широкие бердыши."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3f5e0e90-df66-4388-9907-190790c6b816",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba49c5d1-e9fd-334f-a181-1ff4de32e169",
                        "source_sense_id": "d8415324-71df-3bac-8475-3cd41fe45e52",
                        "target_lang_word": "flail",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "flail",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb153edd-f25f-34ca-9ae5-981a6772218e",
                                        "entry_id": "52ae85e0-8a6b-30ed-9e2f-8d019dc07f81",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tool used for threshing, consisting of a long handle (handstock) with a shorter stick (swipple or swingle) attached with a short piece of chain, thong or similar material."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e54a7249-fbed-4378-9fb3-a404f6f4a908",
                                                "sense_id": "eb153edd-f25f-34ca-9ae5-981a6772218e",
                                                "text": "When in one night, ere glimpse of morn,\nHis shadowy flail hath threshed the corn\nThat ten day-labourers could not end;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "326ba82b-e31f-421f-a39f-0d79989e627d",
                                                "sense_id": "eb153edd-f25f-34ca-9ae5-981a6772218e",
                                                "text": "Huge fragments vaulted like rebounding hail,\nOr chaffy grain beneath the thresher's flail"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "701ba35d-b29d-44c5-ac01-24b8db7c2c00",
                                                "sense_id": "eb153edd-f25f-34ca-9ae5-981a6772218e",
                                                "text": "On him alone the curse of Cain\nFell, like a flail on the garnered grain,\nAnd struck him to the earth!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eff25c9f-c42d-423a-a4fe-3acbd010f50a",
                                                "sense_id": "eb153edd-f25f-34ca-9ae5-981a6772218e",
                                                "text": "If the farmer must use the spade because he has not capital enough for a plough, the sickle instead of the reaping machine, the flail instead of the thresher..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f67f3e4e-31e0-35a5-a4ce-58ba45175511",
                                        "entry_id": "52ae85e0-8a6b-30ed-9e2f-8d019dc07f81",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A weapon which has the (usually spherical) striking part attached to the handle with a flexible joint such as a chain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d56f2e76-b227-3513-85f3-ad965ee4b84f",
                                        "entry_id": "52ae85e0-8a6b-30ed-9e2f-8d019dc07f81",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Part of a rotating device, often used for cutting vegetation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "often",
                                            "plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5b33445-9612-4584-bbb4-fd8dcadb7d60",
                                                "sense_id": "d56f2e76-b227-3513-85f3-ad965ee4b84f",
                                                "text": "The carriage washing plant uses four pairs of rotating rag flails and will be capable of dealing with the whole of the diesel units as well as steam stock used for main-line trains."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "flail",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72326df5-944e-37ed-be48-34bb414196ac",
                                        "entry_id": "3306207c-a40c-3168-af72-676a6cfd02dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To beat using a flail or similar implement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df750955-83fd-341e-910a-aaa657f53344",
                                        "entry_id": "3306207c-a40c-3168-af72-676a6cfd02dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To wave or swing vigorously"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb4e1296-cc34-4c98-adf7-7b18ac81d0d5",
                                                "sense_id": "df750955-83fd-341e-910a-aaa657f53344",
                                                "text": "Tangling with Ziv, Cameron caught him with a flailing elbow, causing the Israeli defender to go down a little easily. However, the referee was in no doubt, much to the displeasure of the home fans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cde84d51-f861-4255-b2bc-fa764e4e294f",
                                                "sense_id": "df750955-83fd-341e-910a-aaa657f53344",
                                                "text": "He stopped in his tracks – then, flailing his arms wildly in the air, began to stagger backwards."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "166394b5-4e30-320a-af6e-9d79432f9242",
                                        "entry_id": "3306207c-a40c-3168-af72-676a6cfd02dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To thresh."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74686529-55a0-33ad-9c5c-ab32363e9ab9",
                                        "entry_id": "3306207c-a40c-3168-af72-676a6cfd02dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To move like a flail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cdafcba-7b1c-4666-a7bf-0b34bf469539",
                                                "sense_id": "74686529-55a0-33ad-9c5c-ab32363e9ab9",
                                                "text": "He was flailing wildly, but didn't land a blow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "382f471a-d8e6-4dd8-b0fa-d09939b8428e",
                                                "sense_id": "74686529-55a0-33ad-9c5c-ab32363e9ab9",
                                                "text": "Undismayed he continued to flail with the broken half of it, denting many a helmet[.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2c2f0954-a72a-47f3-96df-60061ff2d039",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba49c5d1-e9fd-334f-a181-1ff4de32e169",
                        "source_sense_id": "d8415324-71df-3bac-8475-3cd41fe45e52",
                        "target_lang_word": "bludgeon",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bludgeon",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "20f226ae-ced5-3856-b547-b8680faac42e",
                                        "entry_id": "531f9f58-1c57-3ed1-ba82-eb54fa334497",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A short, heavy club, often of wood, which is thicker or loaded at one end."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20c7c67b-47eb-4094-b0cc-fb8161555ef7",
                                                "sense_id": "20f226ae-ced5-3856-b547-b8680faac42e",
                                                "text": "We smashed the radio with a steel bludgeon."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bludgeon",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7b945a3-6adb-36d7-9674-58b566749215",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb67499-e645-3c91-bc54-18b7272c6cd7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To strike or hit with something hard, usually on the head; to club."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0e65eb3-52bf-4720-b843-7b324bb78b32",
                                                "sense_id": "d7b945a3-6adb-36d7-9674-58b566749215",
                                                "text": "The apprehended rioter was bludgeoned to death."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19b7861d-5b75-49fa-94ab-7761c92d1a67",
                                                "sense_id": "d7b945a3-6adb-36d7-9674-58b566749215",
                                                "text": "They didn't get shot to death in hold-ups, strangled to death in rapes, stabbed to death in saloons, bludgeoned to death with axes by parents or children or die summarily by some other act of God."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ee8e254-0811-458c-a97c-c45121d8473a",
                                                "sense_id": "d7b945a3-6adb-36d7-9674-58b566749215",
                                                "text": "Thomas Briggs, a senior bank clerk in the City, lived in Hackney, and on 9 July 1864 he was returning there by train from Fenchurch Street after a Saturday spent at work when he was bludgeoned to death in a first-class carriage, probably by a young German tailor named Franz Müller. (Let's hope it was Müller, because he was hanged for it.) And so Briggs was an all-round pioneer: an early commuter and the very first victim of a railway murder."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8fe243e6-6b7f-395c-a15d-524a5cc702e2",
                                        "entry_id": "9bb67499-e645-3c91-bc54-18b7272c6cd7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To coerce someone, as if with a bludgeon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c05ee35f-a6bd-4ce1-94d0-14a4d988ecdb",
                                                "sense_id": "8fe243e6-6b7f-395c-a15d-524a5cc702e2",
                                                "text": "Their favorite method was bludgeoning us with the same old arguments in favor of their opinions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db731b25-829c-4919-b6ee-1952fba95233",
                                                "sense_id": "8fe243e6-6b7f-395c-a15d-524a5cc702e2",
                                                "text": "Gianna Parasini: You've never worked in the corporate world, have you, Commander? You can't bludgeon through bureaucracy.\nShepard: I can bludgeon pretty hard."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
